Make $K$ the subject: $K = \dfrac{P}{L^{2}\rho v^{3}}$.

Base units of each quantity:

- power $P$ (a rate of doing work): $\mathrm{W} = \mathrm{J\,s^{-1}} = \mathrm{kg\,m^{2}\,s^{-3}}$ ;
- $L^{2}$: $\mathrm{m^{2}}$ ;
- density $\rho$: $\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$ ;
- $v^{3}$: $(\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}})^{3} = \mathrm{m^{3}\,s^{-3}}$.

Hence
$$[L^{2}\rho v^{3}] = \mathrm{m^{2}\times kg\,m^{-3}\times m^{3}\,s^{-3}} = \mathrm{kg\,m^{2}\,s^{-3}}$$
$$[K] = \frac{\mathrm{kg\,m^{2}\,s^{-3}}}{\mathrm{kg\,m^{2}\,s^{-3}}} = 1$$

**$K$ has no units (it is a dimensionless constant).** This also confirms that the equation is homogeneous. (Physically $K = \tfrac{\pi}{2}C_p$, where $C_p$ is the fraction of the wind power extracted by the turbine, so a pure number.)
